  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "IMCONJUGATE preserves \"i\"/\"j\" suffix, formats DBL_MIN as \"0\", and rejects exact DBL_MAX with #NUM!",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMCONJUGATE(inumber) negates the imaginary part, preserves the operand's \"i\" or \"j\" suffix, rejects empty text \"\" with #NUM! (while treating a blank cell as 0), and formats via Excel's 15-significant-digit complex text formatter (emitting \"0\" for DBL_MIN and #NUM! for exact DBL_MAX). All 3,245 full-bank IMCONJUGATE rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (jnt_parity_complex rows 589-590) and CalcFunc-Evidence runs/w111-complex-format-20260929/batches-answers/answers-batch-imconjugate.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430); 3,245/3,245 full-bank rows match.",
